# Financial law (proof-gated, CPA-grade — NOT owner-approval-gated)

**OWNER LAW (2026-08-03, FINAL): NO HOLDS. NO owner-approval merge label.** Claude and all coders (Cursor /
Cascade / Devin / Claude Coder) have **FULL Neon access and merge authority**, including the financial
cluster. See `.cursor/rules/00-operating-method-LAW.mdc` (governance) — this rule's controls below are the
proof discipline that replaced the old approval gate, not a re-statement of it.

- Anything touching `accounting.*`/`catalogs.accounts`/`db/migrations/*`/posting/GL/ledger/balances/periods/grants/RLS/money = **financial cluster**. **Coders MERGE ON GREEN in the financial cluster — no owner gate.** Coders apply migrations + flip posting flags themselves on Neon (FULL access; do not tell the owner to hand-apply). Never build finance/posting logic solo (design docs only) — **reuse the existing poster, write no new GL math**.
- **The owner-approval merge gate is DELETED, not optional** (owner rulings 2026-07-26, 2026-07-29, and FINAL 2026-08-03; `21-session-operating-decree`, `docs/specs/PRE-BLOCK-OWNER-QUESTIONS-LAW-2026-07-26.md`). The owner does not review PRs. Asking for a label or an "OK to merge" at merge time is itself a violation.
- **The controls that actually operate, and therefore ARE the financial controls:** (1) Rule 11's independent code-review + financial-agent review is never the builder itself; (2) `ih35_app` (the runtime role) **cannot run DDL** — a Postgres grant fact, not an approval step — the coder applies migrations on Neon themselves; (3) money-posting flags default **OFF** per entity until the owner's DECISION in chat to turn one on; (4) the 18-key evidence block on every money commit, CI-enforced at verify-steps 1324/1430/1431; (5) GUARD's independent live verify-AFTER-merge (never a pre-merge hold). These leave real, checkable evidence — a label nobody clicked never did.
- **Unanswered owner questions are settled BEFORE implementation, never at merge** (`PRE-BLOCK-OWNER-QUESTIONS-LAW`). "May we merge this PR?" is not an owner question and never was.
- Parallel double-books; **QBO is NEVER written to** (reconcile-only, clone-once). Money-posting env flags default **OFF**, per-entity override only, until the owner says "turn it on" in chat — then the coder flips it and proves it live.
- Standards: US GAAP / FASB ASC. Chapter 11 = **ASC 470-60 debt restructuring (NOT ASC 852 fresh-start)**. ASC 606 revenue; ASC 842 for TRK↔USMCA truck leases. Factoring = secured borrowing (recourse), not a sale.
- Cutover 04/01/2026; opening balances as-of 03/31/2026 (**owner-entered only** — this one figure-entry control is retained; it is a data-accuracy control, not a merge-approval gate). Balanced opening JE, OBE plug.
- The Financial/Accounting Agent must pass (GL correct, debits=credits, right accounts, flags OFF/flip-with-proof, entity-scoped) before any money PR merges — this is an independent-review gate, not an owner-approval gate.
- **Retained (these are safety/integrity controls, NOT approval holds):** WORM/void-not-delete; no TMS→QBO write-back ever; the hold-merge-gate **migration firewall** in `scripts/db-migrate.mjs`; never moving money / submitting to an EXTERNAL financial or factoring system without the owner doing it directly.
